  "description": "Lamar Jackson was the last pick of round one in 2018, was told to switch to wide receiver, then won a unanimous MVP and a five year, 260 million dollar contract.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Lamar Jackson: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamar_Jackson\n- Wikipedia: 2018 NFL draft: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_NFL_draft\n\nFrom the cited pages: the Ravens picked him 32nd overall, the final pick of the first round, in the 2018 NFL draft; many draft pundits suggested he switch to wide receiver but he insisted on playing quarterback; he was the 2019 AP MVP by unanimous vote, the second player after Tom Brady in 2010; on April 27, 2023 he signed a five-year contract worth $260 million $52 million per year; he won a second MVP for the 2023 season; in 2019 he was the second player after Tom Brady in 2010 to be voted MVP unanimously (his first full season). Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #lamarjackson #nfl #howtheymakemoney",
